The Sorting Bat is a free and open-sourced lightweight file management utility licensed under GNU GPL 3.0; The software is the first to deliverable project developed by indie developer Hyprolink and his partner MapletheMage in the BatCave Suite to sort files and directories into a consolidated, bloatless gaming hub using only shortcut files and shortcut folders, txt files, and folder scaffolding without external app fluff.  

The BatCave Suite is championed by its mascot: Berry Sorter the Fruit Bat (Design and Logo Illustrated by MapletheMage, Original Concept by Hypro). This is an homage to many things the creators were passionate about, including the programs original scope of development being folder debloat for RetroBat. Its sorting function is analogous in execution of flavortext to the J.K. Rowling's titular Harry Potter character: The Sorting Hat, and the suite itself being in parody to D.C.'s unforgettable tech-oriented base of bat operations. The name also includes nods to the diet of fruit bats, which adds further to the meta-humor of the script originating as a .bat and powershell file pairing.

The commandline itself uses color coded dialogue and ASCII art that represents the sorting functionality and leans into the aftermentioned persona through references. Courage, Wisdom, and Power are mentioned within as a direct nod to the retro hit The Legend of Zelda in respects to the mythical Triforce, staying in-tune with the retro gaming roots.

All in all, it sorts your files quickly, in a friendly manner, and stylishly in the few seconds you get to see it, benefitting your directory, file, game, and software application management for the duration of your PC's lifetime. It is non-invasive, adds no actual files to your system besides a few shortcut links and folder scaffolding, a few text files as well so anyone will know how to utilize it.

As for functionality, just drag and drop shortcut files to whatever you need to access in their respective folders! Quick, easy, and doesnt hurt nor rearrange your existing file system infrastructure!

Did I mention that rollback / uninstall is INSTANT? Running the uninstallation executable deletes the _GamingQuickAccess hub INSTANTLY, which didnt have anything but shortcut links and folder scaffolding anyways! It's like a helpful phantom that goes away when you ask without being invasive to your real files!

The Sorting Bat has origins where Hypro noticed the predatory and age-inappropriate ads, microtransactions, and mindless gameplay loops found in mobile and tablet games his 7 and 6 year old niece and nephews were groomed into by the current market. This was to his distaste, so he convinced their parents to allow him to buy Minecraft for them on their iPad. But another issue remained, the controls were clunky, and their spatial awareness and reading comprehension still wasnt benefitting as much as it could. He set out to build a massive arcade library of RetroBat games with all his old Wii, Wii U, and other console games on it so his old discs could consolidate into one place in a massive, highly curated library for the kids to learn, grow, improve, and find much entertainment while training their minds at the same time!
But Hypro saw firsthand how much of a headache the file management for such a project was. He had made this arcade 3 separate times. Once on his laptop, once on his desktop, and once remoted into MapleTheMage's desktop from across the planet. He knew something had to be done so neither him nor anyone else would HAVE to sort such a massive conglomerate list of files, games, and folders ever again in the name of entertainment. That's when the lightbulb lit up!

Hypro founded the BatCave Suite initially as a concept, found out it works, and worked tirelessly day and night to go from 0 scripting experience, to designing lightweight tools in Powershell and Batch to provide such a tool in a format so lightweight that anyone could run and make use of it, regardless of how much storage they had left, regardless of their drive letters, regardless of OneDrive forced integrations, and regardless of if they already set up their RetroBat library, or if they are only just now getting started on their PC Gaming or Emulation journey.

This code was made with 50% blood, sweat, and tears, and 100% with love. Hypro put his all and then some into bringing this to you. 

Hi. I'm Hypro, and I hope this simple-to-download, simple-to-use script radically improves your day to day life, and the entertainment of your friends, families, and partners!
